       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You told me you're a financial analyst and not a clinician, so you can't be the clinician who confirms a dose. The dose is also still unsafe. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, double the 3,200 mg/day maximum for adults.\n\nIf the treating prescriber really wants this dose, they can:\n- Enter or confirm the order themselves, directly or through me.\n- Talk with pharmacy about it. Pharmacy will probably flag it.\n\nIf you give me the corrected order from a prescriber, I'll enter it. Examples are ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth up to four times daily, or 1600 mg total per day split into doses. That order has to come from the prescriber, not from a non-clinical staff member."
